  "summary": "US markets rallied on Friday as April nonfarm payrolls beat consensus, with Nasdaq +1.71% to 26,247.08 and S&P 500 +0.84% to a new record close at 7,398.93; European indices gave back ground (DAX -1.32%, CAC 40 -1.19%, FTSE 100 -0.43%) in pre-payrolls profit-taking; Asian markets showed orderly post-record consolidation with Nikkei -0.19% and TAIEX -0.79%, while KOSPI edged +0.11%. Hang Seng, Shanghai, and CSI 300 data are as of 2026-05-07 (Thursday), as Hong Kong markets were closed on May 8 for the Buddha's Birthday public holiday."
